        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6a7ad934-756a-522b-9d87-cb6e7e5d41f8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kevin DuBrow, Lance King, David Ellefson\n- Organizations: Quiet Riot, Nightmare, Megadeth\n- Products: QR III, Terrified, From the Depths of Time\n- Roles: heavy metal singer, vocalist, bassist, record label founder\n\nFacts:\n- Kevin DuBrow was an American heavy metal singer born on October 29, 1955, and he died on November 19, 2007.\n- Kevin DuBrow was the lead vocalist of Quiet Riot from 1975 to 1987 and again from 1990 until his death in 2007.\n- Lance King, born on November 23, 1962, is an American heavy metal vocalist specializing in melodic rock, progressive metal, and power metal.\n- Lance King founded the record label Nightmare in 1990 to release his own music and continues to lead the label.\n- QR III was the last album to feature lead singer Kevin DuBrow until the 1993 album Terrified.\n- The album From the Depths of Time features American vocalist Lance King and then-former Megadeth bassist David Ellefson.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
